# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>

# Type must be one of:
#   feat:     New features                    → MINOR release (0.X.0)
#   fix:      Bug fixes                       → PATCH release (0.0.X)
#   perf:     Performance improvements        → MINOR release (0.X.0)
#   docs:     Documentation changes           → No release
#   style:    Code style changes              → No release  
#   refactor: Code refactoring                → No release
#   test:     Test additions or changes       → No release
#   build:    Build system changes            → No release
#   ci:       CI configuration changes        → No release
#   chore:    Other changes (dependencies)    → No release
#   revert:   Reverting previous commits      → Depends on reverted commit

# Scope is optional but recommended:
#   Examples: ui, api, auth, db, ci, docs

# Subject line:
#   - Use imperative mood ("add" not "added")
#   - Keep under 50 characters
#   - Don't end with period
#   - Start with lowercase letter

# Body (optional):
#   - Explain what and why vs. how
#   - Wrap at 72 characters
#   - Leave blank line between subject and body

# Footer (optional):
#   - Include breaking changes: "BREAKING CHANGE: <description>" → MAJOR release (X.0.0)
#   - Reference issues: "Closes #123", "Fixes #456"
#   - Security fixes: "SECURITY: Fixes CVE-YYYY-XXXX"

# Examples:
#   feat(auth): add OAuth2 integration                → MINOR release
#   fix(api): handle null response in user endpoint   → PATCH release
#   fix(security): patch authentication bypass        → PATCH release (urgent)
#   perf(db): optimize query performance by 60%       → MINOR release  
#   docs: update README with installation steps       → No release
#   build: upgrade gradle to version 8.5              → No release
#   feat!: drop support for Node.js 16                → MAJOR release
#   
#   Breaking change alternative syntax:
#   feat(api): redesign session management
#   
#   BREAKING CHANGE: Session token format changed     → MAJOR release